{"id":"gate:c2d833226c3e1995:codex:gpt-6.1-sol","purpose":"plan","blueprintSlug":"setup-wp-account-auth","subjectScheme":"wp-blueprint-v1","subjectDigest":"53bcdb287a9840dea60d8d01ecf2bbf5db7c9fd71a8b810ff6cc438f908cd8c8","reviewedVersion":"bpv1:9ee9888a366afdb09b45fe39797dd91f4d8f9546a099e4433b06427e2bf7ef58","reviewedCommit":"41295181a58126cbcad595c9bd53ca066ad66c0f","gateId":"c2d833226c3e1995","promptHash":"e43669072a8a588b18a2b2727ae36a2f89b7ecd9b706c8859ba80b74f08f9e2d","reviewer":"codex","providerCorrelationId":"review-gate-c2d833226c3e1995-1-codex-2f9d16c6b8d4","provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","effort":"medium","stage":"approval-gate","status":"complete","verdict":"reject","terminalClassification":"rejected","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:52:06.626Z","artifactPath":"review-artifacts/c2d833226c3e1995-codex-codex.md","artifactSha256":"0778fe5c57c36783cb28c82d25c1b758edaf01708c8ccac2451ce7c105292ccf","schemaVersion":3,"structuredReview":{"schemaVersion":1,"summary":"Two blockers remain: the entitlement-file symlink check occurs after a possible redirected write, and the break-glass output assertion conflicts with the fixture and replay contract. Dimension review: (1) feasibility/internal consistency—output-contract blocker; (2) dependencies/sequencing/ownership—no blocker; (3) acceptance criteria—output-contract blocker; (4) verification of success/failure/cancellation/regression—symlink protection blocker; (5) rollout/compatibility/cleanup—no blocker; (6) unresolved assumptions—no blocker.","findings":[{"severity":"blocker","title":"Reject an existing entitlement-file symlink before invoking wp","location":"Task 1.1 cases (i) and (n); Summary and D3 pre-sign-in filesystem checks","trigger":"RUNNER_TEMP/webpresso/auth is a real directory, but its existing entitlement.jwt is a symlink to a file outside RUNNER_TEMP.","impact":"The prescribed preflight accepts this layout. If wp follows the existing file symlink when writing the entitlement, the token reaches the external destination before the post-sign-in check rejects it. Whether wp independently prevents this is unspecified; the action's stated containment guarantee therefore depends on an unprovided safeguard.","fix":"Before invoking wp, reject an existing entitlement.jwt that is a symlink or any non-regular file. Add a pre-existing file-symlink case asserting that wp is never invoked and the external target remains unchanged. Retain the post-sign-in check.","confidence":"high"},{"severity":"blocker","title":"Reconcile the break-glass test with captured output replay","location":"Task 1.1 stub behavior and case (f); D12","trigger":"The prescribed stub prints the imported entitlement, and setup-wp prints the captured output after registering its mask.","impact":"Case (f) requires the entitlement never to appear in any other output line. A bash-level test sees the raw replayed token because GitHub's log masking does not run in that harness. The required green suite conflicts with the specified implementation, even though mask-before-replay ordering can be correct.","fix":"Make case (f) assert that the mask precedes every replayed token occurrence, while retaining the prohibitions on argv and GITHUB_ENV exposure. Alternatively, require explicit redaction before replay and test that behavior. State clearly whether assertions examine raw process output or runner-rendered logs.","confidence":"high"}]}}
